What are Short Chain Alpha Olefins?
Short-chain alpha olefins (C4-C8) are straight-chain hydrocarbons with double bonds positioned at the α-carbon (terminal carbon). These compounds, including 1-butene, 1-hexene, and 1-octene, serve as critical comonomers in polyolefin production, enhancing material properties such as flexibility and impact resistance. Their high reactivity and purity make them indispensable for manufacturing LLDPE, HDPE, and specialty polymers. Global consumption is estimated at 5.5-6 million tons annually, with prices ranging between USD 700-1100 per ton.
